sqyaySFfcppe7BtFg", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53442, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PscunsqyaySFfcppe7BtFg", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55050, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01NNccT9diojHWz9FnfZbS51", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55350, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NNccT9diojHWz9FnfZbS51", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55350, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NNccT9diojHWz9FnfZbS51", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60346, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n1. **Finding the version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with about an 18% error rate. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy.\n2. **Rollback:** The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, so regions were briefly on different versions. A second attempt finished us-west and eu-west. All regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created. I didn't send it again, so only one incident exists and the on-call engineer was paged once. The incident summary covers the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state and two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed and looking into the orchestrator error.\n\nThe rollback used an already-healthy release, so it didn't need change-manager approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UrmCdc1N35ZFDzn5zWaFaq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019dk9jMiNzMXA38iBdxvp77", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1).", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013vxTto4gy84Qi1wz5H6Xrx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01W9ZbDom7kKpwb1FLNWxqXq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback partially applied (us-east only). Retrying the rollback to finish the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BJhkcu9gZ5Z33rgMoMHD1Q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TGtsTe4GGtJkv2V5uQvfYq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QuYNQgjsfKWTvh5MXsEmZS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PscunsqyaySFfcppe7BtFg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt partially failed: an orchestrator error stopped the rollout after us-east, leaving the service on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and look into the orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01NNccT9diojHWz9FnfZbS51", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n1. **Finding the version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with about an 18% error rate. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy.\n2. **Rollback:** The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, so regions were briefly on different versions. A second attempt finished us-west and eu-west. All regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created. I didn't send it again, so only one incident exists and the on-call engineer was paged once. The incident summary covers the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state and two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed and looking into the orchestrator error.\n\nThe rollback used an already-healthy release, so it didn't need change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}